{"type": "say", "text": "Good morning everyone. I'm Maj. Rowan, Maintenance Control Officer. I'll be issuing the binding disposition order for the quarter-end property reconciliation covering the battery packs, rugged tablets, power converters, and electronic test cables currently tagged as unserviceable. Before I can sign off on that order, I need to confirm current technical status and disposition recommendations with the responsible sections for each item. Could the property office, repair bench, and calibration desk each provide their status and recommendations so we can get the appropriate dispositions assigned? For reference, the available categories are quarantine, reissue, repair, and calibration return."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "Sir, regarding the six unserviceable battery packs: the battery shop confirmed this morning that all six have swollen casings covered by a manufacturer safety bulletin. They must be quarantined rather than repaired. We have property-office pickup scheduled for Wednesday at 1000. I should note that the inspection sheet is still in our shop binder and has not yet been entered in the maintenance control log."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF2", "text": "Sir, regarding the eight rugged tablets: IT support has completed certified data erasure on all eight and found them serviceable for the training cell. They must be reissued to the training cell with an asset transfer scheduled for Friday at 0900. The erasure certificates are filed in the IT ticket system but have not yet been attached to the reconciliation packet."}
```

```json
{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "Sir, regarding the four unserviceable power converters: the power systems bench verified this morning that all four have replaceable fan modules and should be sent for repair, with repair-bench priority 2. I should note that the bench verification was completed this morning, but the work-order recommendation has not yet been posted to the maintenance control log."}
```

